WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
This video contains images of a
preserved, severed human toe.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.910
Just warning you.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.350
There's not really much I can say here.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.541
I'm in Dawson City, which is an old
mining town in the Yukon Territory,

00:00:10.541 --> 00:00:13.480
where the Klondike and Yukon rivers
meet, and this...

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.697
this is a cocktail
with a severed human toe in it.

00:00:16.697 --> 00:00:22.330
- The Sourtoe Cocktail, it's real simple:
straight shot of liquor, at least 40%,

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.350
and you drop a human toe into it.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.950
It all started way back
in Prohibition era.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.900
Two brothers running
alcohol up into Alaska.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.180
They thought the police
were on their trail,

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.980
so one of the brothers
stepped through some water,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.370
got frostbite on his toe.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.380
The other brother took an axe,
hacked off the toe.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.120
They left it in a jar of their alcohol
out in a cabin in the woods.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.590
Years later, Captain Dick
Stevenson bought this cabin,

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.550
was emptying it out and he found
this jar with a toe in it,

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.000
thought it'd be hilarious to
bring it to the bar,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.300
and do some drinks with it
with his friends,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.810
and the Sourtoe Cocktail was born.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:59.880
Our toes we receive from donors,
mostly anonymous,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.440
but we actually have a
gentleman over in the UK right now

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.500
who ran the Yukon ultra-marathon
over the winter, got frostbite,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.910
and decided, you know what?

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.220
Might as well put these
frostbitten, removed toes

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.810
to good use, so we're having
somebody pick them up in June,

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.500
and hopefully, he can
come back here someday

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.450
and do his own toes
in a Sourtoe Cocktail.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.780
Terry Lee is our current Sourtoe Master.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.780
Former ferryboat captain, so he's
got his title of captain there.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.350
Fun guy, loves his toes.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.010
- I serve four nights a week.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.580
I've been doing this for five years,
and I've seen all kinds of people.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.800
This toe is a hammertoe,
which was deformed,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.400
and so it had to be removed.
Who it was removed from, I don't know.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.260
The person is probably still alive,
but for most cases, it's people that's dead.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.540
That's toe number 13.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:52.400
The other toes, you know, one was lost
and a couple were stolen, returned...

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.730
Some just get used up.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:57.230
Five were swallowed, one on purpose,

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.200
and I don't even want
to talk about that guy.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.730
They've gone through quite a life.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.085
- Full disclosure, I don't drink alcohol,

00:02:03.085 --> 00:02:04.690
so there's a little bit of
special dispensation here.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.510
I still have the shot of liquor
and the toe's still going in it,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.770
but I'm pouring off the liquor,

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.810
and putting the toe in
some ginger ale instead.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.160
I'm assured it's all within the rules.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.440
- It's safe, I mean, the health inspector
gives us the okay to do it.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.900
It used to be that it
could be done in anything

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:24.420
from milk to pop to champagne to beer,
but in more recent years,

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.480
we're sticking to straight alcohol
that's 40% or higher,

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.800
and that's sort of our way
of appeasing the health inspector

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.680
and making sure this can continue on.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.140
Now that summer's coming on,
it can get pretty busy.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.780
We can do upwards of 50, 60, 70 a night.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:46.740
- Up to now, we are at 77,888,
but that's since June 11, 1995.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:52.660
This toe started in 1973, so
the number could be 100,000.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.540
- I could wax philosophical
for a while on how this

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.130
isn't actually this disgusting.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.210
It's just like having a
bit of beef jerky in there

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.490
that's being used as a garnish.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.570
And actually, the owner of the beef jerky
would be much less likely to consent

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:06.870
than the owner of the toe.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.280
But, I know what you're here for.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.280
Let's do it.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.113
- Okay.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:12.980
So Thomas.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.330
- Yes?
- Are you ready?

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.163
- I am ready.

00:03:15.163 --> 00:03:16.364
- You better be.

00:03:16.364 --> 00:03:18.900
Be warned, the toe must
not enter the mouth

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.880
or be bitten, chewed,
or God forbid, swallowed,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.510
or it's a $2,500 fine.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.030
And so, in light of the
above, you can drink it fast,

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.880
you can drink it slow, but your lips

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.990
must touch this gnarly toe.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.803
Just your lips, no teeth,
no tongue, no tonsils.

00:03:36.338 --> 00:03:37.171
- Here goes.

00:03:37.171 --> 00:03:38.900
Alright, pour out the liquor.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.433
Pour out the toe.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.733
- There we go.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.703
- Cheers.

00:03:45.703 --> 00:03:46.963
- Make sure it touches the lips.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:49.783
And there it is.

00:03:51.713 --> 00:03:52.910
Well done, sir.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.140
- [shudders]

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.330
- This is the certification
of your folly, sir.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.880
- Thank you very much.

